<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The plate behind a channel logo.

    It used to be white, on the reasoning that logos are drawn for white
    backgrounds. Most IPTV logo packs are the opposite: white lettering on
    transparent, meant for a dark guide - so MSG, MSGSN and a good many others
    were white on white and looked like empty boxes. They had loaded perfectly.

    Dark suits both. White lettering shows plainly, and the coloured marks that
    do exist - a red MOTORTREND, a blue MASN - read at least as well on this as
    they did on white. A genuinely black logo is the one case that loses out,
    and those are rare enough to live with.

    Tried and rejected: choosing the colour per logo by measuring its
    brightness. It looked clever and behaved badly.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="#20242B" />
    <corners android:radius="4dp" />
</shape>
